The Australian FFA Bonanza #1 is a [[FFA]] event organised for the Australian QuakeWorld scene by {{Player|dracs|flag=au}}. The event was inspired by the recent FFA action seen in the [[The Great Quakeholio Tournament 4|QuakeHolio tournament]] and was initiated by {{Player|dracs|flag=au}} to reignite an again, very quiet QuakeWorld scene in Australia mid 2021.  On the day that it was announced, arguably Australia's best player of all time {{Player|Reload|flag=au}} signed up, as did Australia's leading 4on4 player {{Player|Yeti|flag=gb}}.  What followed was unimaginably exciting. Oldschoolers such as {{Player|Mucka|flag=au}} and {{Player|dEF|flag=au}} signed up, together with some of Australia's finest players to have ever played the game in {{Player|Venom|flag=au}}, {{Player|HarlsoM|flag=au}} & {{Player|KF|flag=au}}. Rounding out the entries was Australian GetQuad Nations Cup representative, and DM2 Showdown finalist {{Player|Swoop|flag=ie}}, together with the class of LG kenya specialist {{Player|Profanum|flag=au}} and Australia's most improved player in the last 12 months, {{Player|Moksha|flag=au}}.

The map pool selected is a combination of some of the original deathmatch maps, together with some old favourites that the Australian players grew to love in their prime. 

===Format===
* Timelimit: 10 minutes
* Fraglimit: 120
* Powerups: ON
* DropQuad: ON
* Entry Fee: $10
===Prize Pool===
Winner is decided by total number of frags combined from all maps, not total map wins.
